1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,131
Ninety-one steps.

2
00:00:02,731 --> 00:00:07,733
That's how many Tullia climbed every morning, with a jar of water on her shoulder.

3
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:13,099
It was heavy. The fountain was three streets away.

4
00:00:13,699 --> 00:00:17,258
But the old widow on the top floor could no longer walk.

5
00:00:19,358 --> 00:00:24,414
Julia never thanked her. Not once. She only ever said one thing.

6
00:00:25,014 --> 00:00:26,124
You're late.

7
00:00:27,024 --> 00:00:30,389
Every... single... day.

8
00:00:32,489 --> 00:00:34,444
Then one winter, Julia died.

9
00:00:35,044 --> 00:00:40,125
The landlord found Tullia on the stairs, and handed her a small cloth bundle.

10
00:00:40,725 --> 00:00:42,670
She said this was yours.

11
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:49,493
Inside were coins. Years of them. Every coin Julia had saved.

12
00:00:50,093 --> 00:00:53,988
And a broken piece of pottery, with a few words scratched into it.

13
00:00:56,088 --> 00:01:00,782
You were always late... so I always knew you'd come.

14
00:01:03,082 --> 00:01:05,685
Some people never learn how to say thank you.

15
00:01:06,285 --> 00:01:10,358
So they say it the only way they can... by waiting for you.
